{#
    A value that is shown and not offered — ADR 0013's sixteenth key, and the fallback for
    everything else.

    THREE DIFFERENT THINGS LAND HERE, and that they share one fragment is deliberate:
    a field the entity marks `readonly`, a value the core computes (`virtualjoin`), and a widget
    key that has no fragment yet or none at all — a relation before 002-007-0004, a file before
    story 003-004, a 22nd type from a plugin. In every one of those cases an input would be a
    control whose value this package cannot form correctly, and `FormController::writable()`
    keeps all of them out of the save path, so nothing here can be written by a hand-crafted post
    either.

    The dash belongs to this case alone. `FormController::value()` answers the empty string for
    anything it cannot print, and in an input that would be a value an editor could save by
    accident.

    ONE OF THE THREE SAYS SO SINCE 007-001-0006. For the first two — a field marked `readonly`
    and a computed value — showing the value is the whole and correct answer. For the third it
    was a silent omission: an unsupported type was indistinguishable from an empty field, so an
    editor looking for a missing input had no way to learn that none exists. `field.unsupported`
    is the only one of the three that is a gap, and it now names itself and the type.

    THE VALUE STAYS ABOVE THE HINT. Whoever reads this still needs to see what is stored — the
    hint explains why there is nothing to type in, it does not replace the content.
#}
{% include 'widget/_label.html.twig' %}
            <p class="admin-form__display" id="field-{{ field.property }}">{{ field.value ?: '—' }}</p>
{% if field.unsupported|default(false) %}
            <p class="admin-form__unsupported" role="note">Für den Feldtyp
                <code>{{ field.type|default('(ohne Typangabe)') }}</code> gibt es in dieser
                Oberfläche kein Bedienelement — der Wert wird angezeigt, aber nicht zum Bearbeiten
                angeboten. Ein Projekt kann dafür ein eigenes Bedienelement hinterlegen.</p>
{% endif %}
